  {"name":"@PART1_DIALOGUE_ROLE_MAP_TEXT","visible":true,"text":"(M = Mike; D = Daisy)","font":"SourceHanSansSC-Medium","size":58.3333282470703,"color":"221815","bounds":[300,2921,822,2983]},
  {"name":"@PART1_DIALOGUE_INTRO_TEXT","visible":true,"text":"Mike is in Vienna with his girlfriend Daisy.","font":"SourceHanSansSC-Medium","size":58.3333282470703,"color":"221815","bounds":[299,2777,1367,2839]},
  {"name":"@PART1_READING_LEFT_TEXT_STYLE_SOURCE","visible":true,"text":"                                                         [ ˈfevərɪt] [ˈpæsˌtaɪm]          [ɔl ˈovɚ ðə wɜrld]      \rListening to music is the favorite  pastime of many people all over\r                \r                                [ɪˈspɛʃəlɪ]                                                           [vɪˈɛnə]             \rthe world. This is especially true for people living in Vienna, the city of \r    \r                                                        [ˈmozɑrt]                                    [ˈbɝθˌples]         [ˈklæsɪkḷ]\rsong. Being the home of Mozart, this city is the birthplace of classical\r                                  [wɔlts] \rmusic and the waltz.\r\r\r                            [fɪlz ði ɛr]                                                                [ˈkɑnsɚts]  \rMusic fills the air in Vienna. Going to public concerts is often free\r\r      [tʃɑrdʒ]                                                                                                                         [ˈfeməs]\rof charge. And don’t forget, Vienna is also home to the world famous \r\r                                [kwaɪr]                                                      [ˈɔstrɪə]                      [əˈlaɪv]\rVienna Boys’ Choir. No wonder people say Austria is always alive with\r\rthe sound of music.\r","font":"GentiumPlus","size":58.3333282470703,"color":"622180","bounds":[300,857,2109,2487]},
  {"name":"@PART1_READING_RIGHT_TEXT_STYLE_SOURCE","visible":true,"text":"                                                          [hævɪŋ ðə taɪm ʌv maɪ laɪf]                 \rD: Are you kidding? I’m having the time of my life. I loved the concerts.\r                                         [fænˈtæstɪk]\rM: Concert going is fantastic but what else can we do?\r      [baɪkɪŋ]                      [bæŋks]\rD: Biking along the banks of the river Danube could be fun.\r\rM: It sounds like a great idea!\r\rD: Let’s do it then.\r                                                                                     [ˈhɛzəˌtets]\rM: You’re right. As they say, “He who hesitates is lost.”","font":"GentiumPlus","size":58.3333282470703,"color":"221815","bounds":[2831,456,4667,1433]},
